      notes: "PURPOSE: Explain the four ways deposits strengthen the bank.\n\nFACILITATION GUIDANCE:\n- The hub and the four reasons build automatically. CLICK A REASON's icon on the wheel to reveal its explanation card; reasons can be clicked in any order, following the class discussion.\n- Start with cheap source of funds. This answers the question from the previous slide.\n- Interest spread: explain NIM in simple terms. The bank earns interest on loans and pays interest on deposits; the gap is its margin.\n- Liquidity: deposits let the bank meet withdrawals and obligations without stress.\n- Lending capacity: more deposits mean more loans, so more assets and income.\n- Ask: \"If two banks lend at the same rate, but one pays less for its deposits, which earns more?\"\n\nSUGGESTED ANSWERS / DEBRIEF POINTS:\n- The bank with the lower cost of deposits earns a higher spread (NIM), so it is more profitable.\n\nCOMMON MISCONCEPTIONS:\n- \"More deposits of any kind are equally good.\" Low-cost CASA deposits improve margins far more than high-cost deposits."
