      notes: "PURPOSE: Show the four practical levers through which every employee contributes to CASA growth.\n\nFACILITATION GUIDANCE:\n- Point to the team illustration: CASA growth is a whole-branch effort, not only the sales team's job.\n- Go through the four levers in order: acquire, build the relationship, cross-sell, retain.\n- For each lever, ask learners for one thing they could do at the branch this week.\n- Stress retention: keeping and reactivating an existing customer costs far less than acquiring a new one.\n\nSUGGESTED ANSWERS / DEBRIEF POINTS:\n- Acquisition: ask every satisfied customer for a referral.\n- Relationship building: help a new customer activate digital banking so the account gets used.\n- Cross-selling: offer a salary account to an employer customer, or a business account to a self-employed customer.\n- Retention: call dormant customers and help them reactivate.\n\nCOMMON MISCONCEPTIONS:\n- \"Opening the account is the finish line.\" An account that is not activated and used adds little to the CASA balance."
