      bgImageUrl: "data:image/png;base64,",
      notes: "PURPOSE: Check recall of key Savings Account facts: Savings Max balance and minor eligibility, the Speciale Activ mandate window, the Speciale Platinum AQB and the Senior Citizen locker waiver.\n\nFACILITATION GUIDANCE:\n- Show the slide with five incomplete statements and a word bank of seven words. Two words are not needed.\n- Read a statement aloud, ask a participant which word completes it, then click: the word glides from the word bank into the blank and a green tick appears.\n- Click 1: \"25,000\" moves into statement 1. Click 2: \"10\" into statement 2. Click 3: \"6\" into statement 3. Click 4: \"3L\" into statement 4. Click 5: \"100%\" into statement 5.\n- Click 6 removes the words that were not needed (1L and 50%). To repeat the activity with another group, restart the slide show.\n\nSUGGESTED ANSWERS / DEBRIEF POINTS:\n- Savings Max: AMB of Rs. 25,000 (or the requisite FD relationship as per branch location).\n- Minors above 10 years can open a self-operated Savings Max account, and an ATM/Debit card can be issued.\n- Speciale Activ: the ACH/SI mandate for the home loan must be set up from this account within 6 months of opening.\n- Speciale Platinum: AQB of Rs. 3L.\n- Speciale Senior Citizen: 100% Locker fee waiver for the 1st year.\n\nCOMMON MISCONCEPTIONS:\n- Rs. 1L is the AQB for Speciale Gold and Senior Citizen, not Speciale Platinum.\n- 50% is the 1st-year locker waiver for Savings Max and Speciale Gold; Senior Citizen gets 100%."
