      title: "Slide 42",
      layout: "content",
      blocks: [],
      bgImageUrl: "data:image/png;base64,",
      notes: "PURPOSE\nCheck whether participants can link each current account facility to the business need it solves.\n\nFACILITATION GUIDANCE\nShow the slide with all five facilities on the left and five needs on the right. Ask the group to decide which need each facility solves before each click. Take a few answers, then click: the facility glides into the slot beside its need and a green tick appears. Repeat for the five facilities. To repeat the activity with another group, restart the slide show.\nAnimation sequence:\nClick 1: Doorstep Banking moves beside \"Reduce the risk of carrying a large sum of cash to or from the branch\"\nClick 2: Corporate Internet Banking moves beside the GST, tax and bulk salary payment need\nClick 3: POS (EDC terminal) moves beside card payments at the counter\nClick 4: Payment Gateway moves beside payments over the internet\nClick 5: Merchant Mobile App moves beside raising an invoice and collecting by UPI or card\n\nSUGGESTED ANSWERS / DEBRIEF POINTS\nDoorstep Banking: reduces the risk of carrying a large sum of cash to or from the branch.\nCorporate Internet Banking: GST and tax payments, bulk salary payments, maker/checker and workflow.\nPOS (EDC terminal): card payments at the counter.\nPayment Gateway: payments when customers purchase over the internet.\nMerchant Mobile App: invoices and collection by UPI or card, over the counter or on home delivery.\n\nCOMMON MISCONCEPTIONS\nA payment gateway and a POS terminal are the same thing (the gateway is for internet purchases; the terminal is for counter payments).\n\nVALIDATION FLAGS\n1) Pairs are taken from the Current Account facilities slides. Business Mobile App is left out to avoid overlap with Merchant Mobile App.\n2) This version uses only click-to-advance motion, so it plays in PowerPoint, PowerPoint for the web and LibreOffice Impress. Items glide into place; they are not dragged by the participant."
